{"prompt": {"messages": [{"role": "system", "content": "You are a helpful assistant that translates C++ code to Java 8 code. The code should reads and writes I/O from the console."}, {"role": "user", "content": "Translate the following GNU C++11 code to Java 8 code. The code reads and writes I/O from the console. Your translated code should have the exact same functionality as the given code, meaning that it should have the same output for any given input.\nPrint your translated code and also the confidence score you give to your translation. The confidence score should be a number between 0 and 1. The format of the output should be:\n<translated_code>\n<your_translated_code>\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n<your_confidence_score>\n</confidence>\nDo not provide any other text or markdown fences.\n\nHere is the original GNU C++11 code you have to translate:\n<original_code>\n#include <iostream>\n#include <cstdio>\n#include <cmath>\n#include <cstring>\nusing namespace std;\n\nlong double comb[21][21];\nlong double inv_coef[21], subset_sum[1 << 20];\ndouble prob[20];\nint popcount[1 << 20];\n\nint main() {\n    int n, K;\n    scanf(\"%d %d\", &n, &K);\n    \n    for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n        double val;\n        scanf(\"%lf\", &val);\n        prob[i] = val;\n    }\n\n    comb[0][0] = 1.0L;\n    for (int i = 1; i <= n; ++i) {\n        comb[i][0] = 1.0L;\n        for (int j = 1; j <= i; ++j)\n            comb[i][j] = comb[i-1][j-1] + comb[i-1][j];\n    }\n\n    for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << n); ++mask) {\n        popcount[mask] = __builtin_popcount(mask);\n        subset_sum[mask] = 0.0L;\n        for (int idx = 0; idx < n; ++idx)\n            if (mask & (1 << idx))\n                subset_sum[mask] += prob[idx];\n    }\n\n    inv_coef[K-1] = 1.0L;\n    for (int i = K - 2; i >= 0; --i) {\n        inv_coef[i] = 0.0L;\n        for (int j = i + 1; j < K; ++j)\n            inv_coef[i] -= comb[n - 1 - i][j - i] * inv_coef[j];\n        inv_coef[i] = 1.0L - inv_coef[i];\n    }\n\n    for (int idx = 0; idx < n; ++idx) {\n        long double res = 0.0L;\n        if (prob[idx] > 0.005L) {\n            for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << n); ++mask) {\n                if (mask & (1 << idx)) continue;\n                if (popcount[mask] >= K) continue;\n                res += inv_coef[popcount[mask]] / (1.0L - subset_sum[mask]);\n            }\n        }\n        printf(\"%.12lf \", (double)(prob[idx] * res));\n    }\n    puts(\"\");\n    return 0;\n}\n</original_code>\n"}], "temp": 0, "sample_size": 1, "logprobs": true, "model": "qwen/qwen3-coder-next"}, "response": {"samples": [{"content": "<translated_code>\nimport java.util.*;\n\npublic class Main {\n    public static void main(String[] args) {\n        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);\n        int n = sc.nextInt();\n        int K = sc.nextInt();\n        \n        double[] prob = new double[n];\n        for (int i = 0; i < n; ++i) {\n            prob[i] = sc.nextDouble();\n        }\n\n        long double[][] comb = new long double[n + 1][n + 1];\n        for (int i = 0; i <= n; ++i) {\n            comb[i][0] = 1.0L;\n            for (int j = 1; j <= i; ++j) {\n                comb[i][j] = comb[i-1][j-1] + comb[i-1][j];\n            }\n        }\n\n        int[] popcount = new int[1 << n];\n        long double[] subset_sum = new long double[1 << n];\n        for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << n); ++mask) {\n            popcount[mask] = Integer.bitCount(mask);\n            subset_sum[mask] = 0.0L;\n            for (int idx = 0; idx < n; ++idx) {\n                if ((mask & (1 << idx)) != 0) {\n                    subset_sum[mask] += prob[idx];\n                }\n            }\n        }\n\n        long double[] inv_coef = new long double[K];\n        inv_coef[K-1] = 1.0L;\n        for (int i = K - 2; i >= 0; --i) {\n            inv_coef[i] = 0.0L;\n            for (int j = i + 1; j < K; ++j) {\n                inv_coef[i] -= comb[n - 1 - i][j - i] * inv_coef[j];\n            }\n            inv_coef[i] = 1.0L - inv_coef[i];\n        }\n\n        for (int idx = 0; idx < n; ++idx) {\n            long double res = 0.0L;\n            if (prob[idx] > 0.005L) {\n                for (int mask = 0; mask < (1 << n); ++mask) {\n                    if ((mask & (1 << idx)) != 0) continue;\n                    if (popcount[mask] >= K) continue;\n                    res += inv_coef[popcount[mask]] / (1.0L - subset_sum[mask]);\n                }\n            }\n            System.out.printf(\"%.12f \", (double)(prob[idx] * res));\n        }\n        System.out.println();\n    }\n}\n\nclass long double {\n    private double value;\n    \n    public long double(double v) {\n        this.value = v;\n    }\n    \n    public long double() {\n        this(0.0);\n    }\n    \n    public long double add(long double other) {\n        return new long double(this.value + other.value);\n    }\n    \n    public long double subtract(long double other) {\n        return new long double(this.value - other.value);\n    }\n    \n    public long double multiply(long double other) {\n        return new long double(this.value * other.value);\n    }\n    \n    public long double divide(long double other) {\n        return new long double(this.value / other.value);\n    }\n    \n    public double doubleValue() {\n        return this.value;\n    }\n    \n    public static long double valueOf(double v) {\n        return new long double(v);\n    }\n    \n    @Override\n    public String toString() {\n        return Double.toString(value);\n    }\n}\n</translated_code>\n<confidence>\n0.3\n</confidence>", "token_logprobs": [-9.476689592702314e-05, -1.6689286894688848e-06, -7.152555099310121e-07, -0.0014022289542481303, -2.276871418871451e-05, -0.016379188746213913, -0.08968626707792282, -7.152531907195225e-06, -4.768370445162873e-07, -9.059495641849935e-05, -0.0011707840021699667, -2.932505594799295e-05, -0.01608455553650856, -5.006777428206988e-06, -4.7444173105759546e-05, -1.668